# What "docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile ." sends to Docker. An allow-list: everything is left out
# first, then only what the image needs is let back in. The repository folder holds gigabytes the
# image must never see (caches, virtual environments, node_modules, the data folders and model
# files of a source checkout). Rules: the last matching line wins; ! lets a path back in.
*

# The program: the Python modules, the routers and the bundled place data, with the package lists
!api/*.py
!api/requirements.txt
!api/constraints.txt
!api/routers
!api/place_data

# The web interface sources (built inside the image)
!app

# The shared install script
!scripts/linux-deps.sh

# Left out again, below the allow-list
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.sqlite3
**/.env
**/.backend.lock
api/tests
api/tools
api/.venv
api/build
api/dist
api/cache
api/chroma_data
api/data
api/models
api/*.spec
**/node_modules
app/dist
app/dist-electron
app/dist-built
app/release
